spec: specs/resilience.md — the adaptive-concurrency box gates on exactly this

why: eight pieces of microservice machinery landed today, each with
  tests, and NOT ONE is wired into a running service. The demo already
  uses okay-ops (lifecycle, RED, /metrics); its Anthropic transport is
  the repo's one live outbound call and has no breaker, no limiter, no
  budget. Wiring it makes the arc a worked instance instead of a shelf,
  and it is what specs/resilience.md names as the obstacle to measuring
  adaptive concurrency.

what: okay-demo depends on okay-resilience; a Breaker + Limiter + a
  per-call budget around the transport it provides, via
  Resilient.guarded (three lines at the edge, which is the design's
  own claim — verify it is really three); the guards' stats join
  /metrics through Ops.routes(guards = ...), which already takes them.
  A test that the demo's guarded transport refuses when the breaker is
  open, over the demo's own scripted model rather than a live one.

next: read how the demo's tests build their fixture, wire, test, gate
